1
00:02:49,002 --> 00:03:18,982
We'll be right back.

2
00:03:19,002 --> 00:03:48,982
We'll be right back.

3
00:03:49,002 --> 00:04:18,982
We'll be right back.

4
00:04:18,982 --> 00:04:25,382
Capture Robin, the determination of the Straw Hats.

5
00:04:29,882 --> 00:04:31,282
Hold it right there!

6
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:32,782
Don't let him get away!

7
00:04:36,282 --> 00:04:38,242
This is all your fault, Zoro!

8
00:04:38,662 --> 00:04:40,482
The whole town is out looking for us.

9
00:04:40,522 --> 00:04:42,722
It was gonna happen sooner or later, wasn't it?

10
00:04:42,882 --> 00:04:44,202
You can't run forever!

11
00:04:45,902 --> 00:04:46,782
This way!

12
00:04:46,982 --> 00:04:47,302
Right!

13
00:04:50,242 --> 00:04:52,662
Over here!

14
00:04:52,662 --> 00:05:01,282
Where'd they go?

15
00:05:01,582 --> 00:05:02,902
Check the alleys!

16
00:05:04,442 --> 00:05:06,702
You don't think they're on the rooftops, do you?

17
00:05:07,442 --> 00:05:08,062
Damn it!

18
00:05:08,162 --> 00:05:08,842
We lost them!

19
00:05:09,522 --> 00:05:10,462
I don't get it.

20
00:05:10,622 --> 00:05:11,862
I'm sure they went this way.

21
00:05:12,262 --> 00:05:13,342
We better keep moving.

22
00:05:13,762 --> 00:05:15,942
All right, but we should check inside the buildings, too.

23
00:05:16,122 --> 00:05:16,462
Good!

24
00:05:16,622 --> 00:05:17,322
We'll split up!

25
00:05:17,562 --> 00:05:18,122
Let's go!

26
00:05:18,462 --> 00:05:18,942
Yeah!

27
00:05:21,742 --> 00:05:23,122
Is it okay now?

28
00:05:23,222 --> 00:05:23,882
Wait a sec.

29
00:05:26,082 --> 00:05:27,362
Where'd you last see them?

30
00:05:27,362 --> 00:05:31,782
Just a little longer.

31
00:05:31,782 --> 00:05:31,802
Just a little longer.

32
00:05:47,802 --> 00:05:48,262
Hmm?

33
00:05:49,102 --> 00:05:50,562
What's that?

34
00:05:50,562 --> 00:06:00,862
I'm begging you.

35
00:06:01,602 --> 00:06:02,842
Are you crazy?

36
00:06:03,102 --> 00:06:04,102
I gotta evacuate.

37
00:06:04,402 --> 00:06:05,542
Stop pestering me.

38
00:06:06,302 --> 00:06:07,082
Come on.

39
00:06:07,602 --> 00:06:08,942
I have money, okay?

40
00:06:10,282 --> 00:06:11,522
Here, take it.

41
00:06:11,782 --> 00:06:14,882
I need as much lumber, tar, and rope as this will buy.

42
00:06:15,302 --> 00:06:18,502
Oh, and also some nails, latches, and tin plates, if you don't mind.

43
00:06:18,822 --> 00:06:20,622
I said I'm closing the shop.

44
00:06:20,902 --> 00:06:22,022
It'll just take a second.

45
00:06:22,342 --> 00:06:22,782
Please.

46
00:06:29,042 --> 00:06:29,962
Okay, kid.

47
00:06:30,162 --> 00:06:32,662
But I'm afraid this money ain't gonna buy much for you.

48
00:06:33,002 --> 00:06:34,342
Uh, then...

49
00:06:34,342 --> 00:06:35,882
How about I sell my tools?

50
00:06:36,122 --> 00:06:37,402
Will that make up for the rest?

51
00:06:37,502 --> 00:06:38,222
Hey, hey!

52
00:06:38,462 --> 00:06:39,702
Come on, stop it.

53
00:06:39,962 --> 00:06:41,142
We don't do barter.

54
00:06:41,282 --> 00:06:42,702
This is the big city, you know.

55
00:06:43,002 --> 00:06:44,782
I'm sorry, but it's cash only.

56
00:06:44,782 --> 00:06:53,682
You win.

57
00:06:53,942 --> 00:06:55,082
But let's make it quick.

58
00:07:02,682 --> 00:07:05,722
You sure you're okay carrying that with all those injuries?

59
00:07:06,942 --> 00:07:09,082
Can't you get some friends to help you out?

60
00:07:09,602 --> 00:07:10,062
Hey!

61
00:07:10,062 --> 00:07:13,982
I knew this was a bad idea.

62
00:07:31,102 --> 00:07:32,962
Wait, this isn't gonna work.

63
00:07:32,962 --> 00:07:34,842
I'm fine.

64
00:07:35,402 --> 00:07:36,102
I got it.

65
00:07:36,442 --> 00:07:37,322
This is nothing.

66
00:07:37,442 --> 00:07:37,762
Hey!

67
00:07:38,122 --> 00:07:38,902
Don't worry.

68
00:07:39,342 --> 00:07:40,262
I can do it.

69
00:07:40,342 --> 00:07:41,022
No, look.

70
00:07:41,702 --> 00:07:42,962
Here, take these.

71
00:07:43,462 --> 00:07:44,402
You're hungry, right?

72
00:07:49,602 --> 00:07:50,362
Thank you.

73
00:07:50,842 --> 00:07:51,542
Sure thing.

74
00:07:52,342 --> 00:07:53,462
Try to be careful.

75
00:07:53,462 --> 00:08:02,042
Good luck out there, kid.

76
00:08:10,842 --> 00:08:11,402
Mmm.

77
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,962
These are good.

78
00:08:14,822 --> 00:08:15,802
Really good.

79
00:08:17,802 --> 00:08:20,242
Guess that guy was pretty nice after all.

80
00:08:20,242 --> 00:08:35,582
The waves sure are getting high, aren't they?

81
00:08:42,162 --> 00:08:43,242
Don't worry, Mary.

82
00:08:43,602 --> 00:08:45,182
You're gonna be just fine.

83
00:08:45,182 --> 00:08:57,202
After all, you flew in the sky, remember?

84
00:08:58,482 --> 00:09:00,722
You got nothing to be afraid of.

85
00:09:00,722 --> 00:09:03,422
You got nothing to be afraid of.

86
00:09:07,682 --> 00:09:08,342
No, no.

87
00:09:09,482 --> 00:09:10,822
Oh, oh, oh.

88
00:09:11,162 --> 00:09:11,722
Whoa.

89
00:09:12,442 --> 00:09:14,342
What's got you riled up, big guy?

90
00:09:14,442 --> 00:09:16,322
Gotta cry.

91
00:09:20,762 --> 00:09:22,022
Oops.

92
00:09:24,062 --> 00:09:26,282
Thank you.

93
00:09:28,422 --> 00:09:28,462
Thank you.

94
00:09:28,502 --> 00:09:29,422
Thanks, mate.

95
00:09:29,422 --> 00:09:33,322
Come on, Frankie, you can tell us.

96
00:09:45,322 --> 00:09:46,342
What's up, bro?

97
00:09:47,782 --> 00:09:52,562
I got so much rage inside me, I feel another rampage coming on right about now.

98
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:55,762
Hey, wait for me, bro. Don't rampage alone.

99
00:09:57,022 --> 00:09:59,162
As always, thanks for the drinks, Bluno.

100
00:09:59,422 --> 00:10:06,922
What got into him all of a sudden? Is there something going on?

101
00:10:11,082 --> 00:10:17,282
Beats me. Never can tell with that guy. Only idiots know what idiots are thinking.

102
00:10:17,282 --> 00:10:32,002
Looks like the crowd cleared out.

103
00:10:32,002 --> 00:10:33,442
Yeah, no thanks to you.

104
00:10:33,862 --> 00:10:39,542
I'll have you know that Luffy and I had a perfectly good hiding place until you led that angry mob straight to us.

105
00:10:39,622 --> 00:10:42,762
Like I said, with that many people looking, they were going to find you anyway.

106
00:10:43,482 --> 00:10:47,002
Oh yeah, that reminds me. How'd you know we were down there, Chopper?

107
00:10:47,162 --> 00:10:47,742
Your smell?

108
00:10:48,442 --> 00:10:52,002
Ah, should have known. But wait, wasn't Sanji with you?

109
00:10:52,002 --> 00:10:54,022
Well, he was.

110
00:11:07,942 --> 00:11:12,002
No way! That doesn't make any sense! Did Robin really say that to you?

111
00:11:12,002 --> 00:11:22,742
We were prepared for this, weren't we?

112
00:11:25,702 --> 00:11:29,942
After all, Robin was our enemy before we let her join the crew.

113
00:11:29,942 --> 00:11:34,442
This might be our only chance to find out the truth, so we shouldn't run away.

114
00:11:37,142 --> 00:11:40,102
There's still a lot of things we don't know about Robin.

115
00:11:40,902 --> 00:11:45,142
Now it's time to decide if she's a friend or a foe.

116
00:11:45,142 --> 00:12:03,622
The situation will get worse.

117
00:12:04,142 --> 00:12:08,142
From this day forward, we will never see each other again.

118
00:12:08,142 --> 00:12:23,102
If she says she won't see us after today and things are going to get worse,

119
00:12:23,262 --> 00:12:26,142
maybe that means the attack on Iceberg was just a warm-up

120
00:12:26,142 --> 00:12:28,522
and she has something even bigger planned for tonight.

121
00:12:28,522 --> 00:12:35,262
I don't know why Robin's doing any of this,

122
00:12:35,362 --> 00:12:37,722
so it's hard to make a guess as to what she's planning.

123
00:12:38,222 --> 00:12:41,402
But seeing how much commotion her first attack on the mayor caused,

124
00:12:41,562 --> 00:12:43,642
there's only one way to make things worse.

125
00:12:44,022 --> 00:12:46,602
In other words, she'll murder him.

126
00:12:49,742 --> 00:12:52,402
I think that's what she's trying to tell us, at least.

127
00:12:53,942 --> 00:12:57,462
Also, since she told Chopper that she'll be pinning the crime on us,

128
00:12:57,462 --> 00:12:59,742
it could be that she's feeding us all these little hints

129
00:12:59,742 --> 00:13:02,042
to try and lure us out to the crime scene tonight.

130
00:13:02,742 --> 00:13:03,422
Think so?

131
00:13:03,902 --> 00:13:06,482
If that is her plan, it would be convenient for her

132
00:13:06,482 --> 00:13:07,782
if we did happen to show up,

133
00:13:07,902 --> 00:13:10,082
since that would put us at the scene of the crime.

134
00:13:10,262 --> 00:13:11,902
You say you don't know what she's thinking,

135
00:13:12,042 --> 00:13:14,902
but it sounds to me like you've already decided that she's our enemy!

136
00:13:15,242 --> 00:13:17,442
I'm talking about possibilities here, that's all.

137
00:13:17,642 --> 00:13:20,562
We should always be prepared for the worst-case scenario, understand?

138
00:13:21,182 --> 00:13:23,502
If I get locked into a single line of thinking,

139
00:13:23,602 --> 00:13:24,762
it'll only slow me down.

140
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:27,842
If she's my friend, I have to be ready to forgive.

141
00:13:28,482 --> 00:13:31,622
But if she's my enemy, I have to be ready to fight.

142
00:13:36,182 --> 00:13:39,002
Our best chance to settle this is tonight.

143
00:13:39,262 --> 00:13:39,942
Are we going?

144
00:13:40,142 --> 00:13:40,802
Of course.

145
00:13:40,802 --> 00:13:52,582
It's not that I object to the plan,

146
00:13:53,142 --> 00:13:54,982
but we're still forgetting something.

147
00:13:56,062 --> 00:13:59,402
Sanji said he saw Robin walking with someone in a mask, remember?

148
00:14:00,302 --> 00:14:01,962
Obviously, that wasn't one of us,

149
00:14:02,042 --> 00:14:04,122
but Iceberg said exactly the same thing,

150
00:14:04,222 --> 00:14:07,042
that he was attacked by Robin and a large man in a mask

151
00:14:07,042 --> 00:14:08,122
that he didn't recognize.

152
00:14:08,122 --> 00:14:11,242
Whoever he is, I bet he's the reason

153
00:14:11,242 --> 00:14:12,922
Robin is doing all of this stuff.

154
00:14:13,002 --> 00:14:14,582
Yeah, that means it isn't our fault

155
00:14:14,582 --> 00:14:16,862
and we just need to be the real bad guy, right?

156
00:14:17,062 --> 00:14:18,522
That's the ideal situation.

157
00:14:19,202 --> 00:14:20,102
But on the other hand,

158
00:14:20,162 --> 00:14:23,042
it's also possible that this guy is one of Robin's friends.

159
00:14:23,262 --> 00:14:25,462
The problem is, we don't have much to go on

160
00:14:25,462 --> 00:14:27,342
other than a big man in a mask.

161
00:14:27,422 --> 00:14:28,722
So where do we even start?

162
00:14:28,942 --> 00:14:30,582
I mean, what is our goal here?

163
00:14:31,122 --> 00:14:32,962
We find Robin and capture her.

164
00:14:32,962 --> 00:14:43,682
That's the only way we'll ever know the truth.

165
00:14:44,962 --> 00:14:45,702
You're right.

166
00:14:46,062 --> 00:14:48,102
We're wasting time here trying to figure it out.

167
00:14:48,582 --> 00:14:49,442
Just one thing,

168
00:14:50,082 --> 00:14:51,602
Robin won't be easy to catch.

169
00:14:52,382 --> 00:14:55,042
After all, the world government's been trying for 20 years

170
00:14:55,042 --> 00:14:56,262
and it still hasn't happened.

171
00:14:57,582 --> 00:14:58,482
Like he said,

172
00:14:58,522 --> 00:15:00,362
it's the only way we'll really know for sure.

173
00:15:02,362 --> 00:15:04,362
Yeah, let's settle this right now.

174
00:15:04,962 --> 00:15:05,442
Right.

175
00:15:06,442 --> 00:15:08,402
Come on, Gallylaw's waiting.

176
00:15:08,402 --> 00:15:16,302
Damn, it's late.

177
00:15:16,542 --> 00:15:18,442
Where'd that straw hat run off to?

178
00:15:18,842 --> 00:15:20,562
Paulie, we gotta go.

179
00:15:21,062 --> 00:15:23,142
All these streets are gonna flood before long.

180
00:15:23,682 --> 00:15:25,482
All right, let's head back.

181
00:15:26,042 --> 00:15:27,502
I'm going to the main office.

182
00:15:27,842 --> 00:15:28,782
Sounds good, boss.

183
00:15:29,342 --> 00:15:30,282
You heard him, guys.

184
00:15:30,282 --> 00:15:31,482
Time to move out.

185
00:15:32,842 --> 00:15:36,282
Get out here and fight me, straw hat!

186
00:15:36,282 --> 00:15:38,902
Where are you?

187
00:15:40,162 --> 00:15:41,042
Stop hiding!

188
00:15:42,982 --> 00:15:45,322
I thought that little turd had some backbone,

189
00:15:45,462 --> 00:15:46,782
but I guess I was wrong.

190
00:15:47,842 --> 00:15:49,462
Won't even show his face.

191
00:15:49,882 --> 00:15:51,402
I know what you're saying, bro,

192
00:15:51,502 --> 00:15:52,242
but to be fair,

193
00:15:52,362 --> 00:15:54,742
the whole island is hunting him down right now, you know?

194
00:15:54,882 --> 00:15:55,322
Exactly.

195
00:15:55,742 --> 00:15:57,982
I bet he's hiding if he hasn't been caught already.

196
00:15:59,002 --> 00:15:59,922
By the way,

197
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,342
what's with this weird crab walk thing all of a sudden?

198
00:16:02,362 --> 00:16:03,322
If we face the front,

199
00:16:03,442 --> 00:16:04,842
then the wind catches our hair,

200
00:16:04,842 --> 00:16:06,502
and we blow away!

201
00:16:08,142 --> 00:16:09,042
Speaking of which,

202
00:16:09,102 --> 00:16:11,622
the weather isn't the only thing that's out of control today.

203
00:16:11,822 --> 00:16:12,662
Tell me about it.

204
00:16:12,702 --> 00:16:15,362
It's like you've got a rampage going on inside you, too.

205
00:16:15,622 --> 00:16:16,462
Shut up.

206
00:16:16,742 --> 00:16:18,462
I'm just like that this week, okay?

207
00:16:19,802 --> 00:16:20,242
Hey!

208
00:16:20,402 --> 00:16:20,882
Bro!

209
00:16:21,462 --> 00:16:22,542
Hey, it's Bro!

210
00:16:22,722 --> 00:16:23,002
Hey, Bro!

211
00:16:23,002 --> 00:16:24,682
Well, if it isn't, Zambai...

212
00:16:24,682 --> 00:16:26,502
Tell me!

213
00:16:26,782 --> 00:16:29,102
Tell me that you beat up those stupid straw hats!

214
00:16:29,242 --> 00:16:30,282
Yeah, but I tried to.

215
00:16:30,282 --> 00:16:31,842
Some angry mops showed up,

216
00:16:31,922 --> 00:16:32,562
got in the way,

217
00:16:32,642 --> 00:16:33,522
then Luffy took off.

218
00:16:33,522 --> 00:16:36,782
Are those guys lucky or what?

219
00:16:37,022 --> 00:16:38,282
When you're on a rampage,

220
00:16:38,382 --> 00:16:39,522
nobody survives!

221
00:16:39,962 --> 00:16:40,662
That's weird.

222
00:16:40,962 --> 00:16:42,162
I wondered why that weak dude

223
00:16:42,162 --> 00:16:42,862
with the long nose

224
00:16:42,862 --> 00:16:44,322
was fixing the ship on his own.

225
00:16:44,502 --> 00:16:45,782
I figured that you'd wrecked up

226
00:16:45,782 --> 00:16:47,002
the rest of the crew so bad

227
00:16:47,002 --> 00:16:48,142
that he was the only one left

228
00:16:48,142 --> 00:16:49,122
who could do anything.

229
00:16:49,822 --> 00:16:50,262
Wait,

230
00:16:50,262 --> 00:16:51,802
you found one of them?

231
00:16:51,942 --> 00:16:52,342
Yeah!

232
00:16:52,842 --> 00:16:54,242
On their ship!

233
00:16:58,622 --> 00:16:59,602
Well, that's just fine,

234
00:16:59,662 --> 00:17:00,782
because all we need is one.

235
00:17:01,742 --> 00:17:02,442
In other words,

236
00:17:02,502 --> 00:17:03,982
we'll use that loser as bait

237
00:17:03,982 --> 00:17:05,242
to lure out the rest of them.

238
00:17:06,202 --> 00:17:06,642
Whoa!

239
00:17:06,822 --> 00:17:08,842
Bro's got his bad guy face on, guys!

240
00:17:08,842 --> 00:17:12,502
All right, you good-for-nothings.

241
00:17:12,502 --> 00:17:13,842
I want you to march through the town

242
00:17:13,842 --> 00:17:15,402
and spread the word for me.

243
00:17:15,902 --> 00:17:16,302
Say,

244
00:17:16,562 --> 00:17:17,902
we've got Long Nose,

245
00:17:17,962 --> 00:17:18,842
and if you don't want him

246
00:17:18,842 --> 00:17:19,882
swimming with the fishes,

247
00:17:20,262 --> 00:17:21,282
then come to the warehouse

248
00:17:21,282 --> 00:17:22,362
under the bridge.

249
00:17:22,662 --> 00:17:23,162
Tell him

250
00:17:23,162 --> 00:17:24,282
Frankie

251
00:17:24,282 --> 00:17:25,502
sent ya.

252
00:17:28,402 --> 00:17:29,422
In the meantime,

253
00:17:29,622 --> 00:17:31,042
I'll go nab Long Nose

254
00:17:31,042 --> 00:17:32,002
so we can make good

255
00:17:32,002 --> 00:17:33,022
on our little threat.

256
00:17:33,482 --> 00:17:34,622
You get it, bro!

257
00:17:34,622 --> 00:17:35,342
I swear

258
00:17:35,342 --> 00:17:36,682
we won't let you down!

259
00:17:57,142 --> 00:17:57,862
Hey, you!

260
00:17:58,262 --> 00:17:59,362
Yeah, you with the luggage.

261
00:17:59,542 --> 00:18:00,702
What's all that stuff you got?

262
00:18:00,822 --> 00:18:02,242
It's my special bed.

263
00:18:02,242 --> 00:18:04,762
Aqualaguda!

264
00:18:05,102 --> 00:18:06,402
Aqualaguda!

265
00:21:55,080 --> 00:22:06,600
疲れ果てた向きの中でも変わらないもの探すコンバスで いつまでも持っていれるから

266
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:13,920
いつか辿り着く夢の終わりに できるだけこのままで大人に

267
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:19,080
見上げた果てしないこの大空に 永遠に 永遠に

268
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:31,060
幼き頃の夢物語 忘られち記憶の糸辿り 未だ胸を焦がす残り火を消してしまわないように

269
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:41,880
